Scan out interlaced FRAME-mode fields at native width and full height (1x)

High-resolution scanout used one scale for width and height, so field-aware
rendering (every field drawn at full height, nothing merged) existed only at
2x and 4x. At 1x a 640 x 256 field was returned and two fields had to be
merged on the CPU, which stripes moving or flashing parts. Add a vertical-only
mode: VSyncInfo::high_resolution_vertical_only keeps the width native and
scales only the height, so with a 2 x 2 (or larger ordered) sample grid a
1x field comes out 640 x 511, aligned like 2x/4x (half-line shift, one line
cropped). sample_circuit.frag reads, per output pixel, the samples the full
high-resolution scanout shows at the same height in the native column, or
averages the columns (high_resolution_vertical_only_average_x). Anything that
is not field-aware (FIELD mode, progressive) falls back to native scanout.
ScanoutResult::high_resolution_scale_x_log2 reports the horizontal scale.
Shader bytecode spliced with tools/parallel_gs_splice_shader.py (both
PROMOTED variants, glslc -O --target-env=vulkan1.1).

Applies on top of 0001, 0002 and 0003 (DW5XL issue 009 v4).

